\chapter{Tokamak MHD Confinement Module}
\label{chap:tokamak}

\section{Introduction}

This chapter presents the tokamak magnetohydrodynamic (MHD) confinement
module, modeling toroidal plasmas under $H_{\text{fusion}}$.

\section{MHD Momentum Equation}

\begin{equation}
\rho\left(
\frac{\partial \mathbf{v}}{\partial t}
+
(\mathbf{v}\cdot\nabla)\mathbf{v}
\right)
=
\mathbf{J}\times\mathbf{B}
-
\nabla P
+
\mu\nabla^{2}\mathbf{v}.
\end{equation}

\section{Plasma Beta}

\begin{equation}
\beta = \frac{P}{B^{2}/(2\mu_{0})}.
\end{equation}

\section{Confinement Stability}

Stability is enforced by maintaining $\beta \approx 0.08$ and suppressing
resistive tearing modes under encrypted evolution $E_{\Lambda}$.

