\chapter{Encryption Tensor Architecture}
\label{chap:encryption}

\section{Introduction}

This chapter details the construction and properties of the symplectic
encryption tensor $E_{\Lambda}$.

\section{Encrypted Evolution Operator}

\begin{equation}
E_{\Lambda}(\mathbf{z})
=
\mathbf{J}^{-1}
\exp\left(
\sum_{k=1}^{n}\lambda_k \hat{H}_k
\right)
\mathbf{z}.
\end{equation}

\section{Symplectic Condition}

\begin{equation}
E_{\Lambda}^{T}\mathbf{J}E_{\Lambda} = \mathbf{J}.
\end{equation}

\section{Generator Algebra}

The set $\{\hat{H}_k\}$ forms a generator basis for encrypted Hamiltonian
flows, preserving invariants defined in Chapter~\ref{chap:axioms}.

